   "content": "<h2 id=\"unit1\">Social Studies Exam Possible Answers</h2>\n<h3>Possible Answers (Ses 7)</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>A) Malawian lakes;</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Malawi, Malombe, Chirwa, Kazuni, Chiuta</p>\n<p>B) Tanzania, Zambia, Mozambique</p>\n<p>C) settlement / good farming activities/ roads made easy</p>\n<p>B) i- you know your status</p>\n<p>- you take precuationally measures (preventive measures)</p>\n<p>ii- unprotected sex</p>\n<p>iii- go for VCT (voluntary counseling and testing)</p>\n<p>34- A- right to education /life/play/protection/ etc</p>\n<p>B- Road traffic commission (department)</p>\n<p>C- i) danger warning signs</p>\n<p>ii- regulatory signs</p>\n<p>iii- informative signs</p>\n<p>D- observing road signs and</p>\n<p>Follow signals eg. Traffic lights</p>\n<p>Police signals</p>\n<p>35- A) Likoma Island</p>\n<p>b) Nkhotakota</p>\n<p>c) Malindi</p>\n<p>B) first mission station was Magomero in Chiradzuu</p>\n<p>C) Charles Macknzie</p>\n<p>36- A) needy children/ prone to problems</p>\n<p>B) food, shelter, school etc education</p>\n<p>C) a public official who has power to decide / one who make solutions</p>\n<p>D) a. Gideon</p>\n<p>b. Samson</p>\n<p>c. Deborah</p>\n<p>d. Jephthah</p>\n<p>37- A) purpose for which people are sent</p>\n<p>B) honest/good decision/ able o interpret the laws etc.</p>\n<p>C) Teachers/ chiefs/ umpires/ referees etc</p>\n<p>D) Joash</p>\n<p>E) Mary</p>\n<p>38- A) only 300 men</p>\n<p>B) to deliver (save) the Israel from the hands of Midianites</p>\n<p>C) Samson was stronger because of un-cut hairs (never been cut)</p>\n<p>D) - cut off his hairs</p>\n<p>- gouged out his eyes</p>\n<p>E) Delilah</p>\n<p>F) Manoah</p>\n<p>D) Chokomekome cha nkhuyu mkati muli nyerere.</p>\n<p>- maonekedwe apusitsa</p>\n<p>E) telling stories / narrating stories/ meanings conveying messages</p>\n<p>F) Adam</p>\n<p>B) repent- to be sorry for wrong done\nC) i- welcomed him\nii- cerebrated by killing a fattened calf\niii- gave him the best lobe (dress)\niv- best oil etc</p>\n<ol>\n<li>It is important to forgive those who repent</li>\n</ol>"
